  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A person of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"50\\; \\textup{kg}\"></span> is sitting on the edge of a rotating disc.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>The diameter of the disc is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4.0\\; \\textup{m}\"></span> and its moment of inertia is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"400\\; \\textup{kg\\,m}^{2}\"></span>. The initial angular velocity of the disc is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.0\\; \\textup{rad\\,s}^{-1}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Given that no external torque acts on the system, what is the work done by the person when she crawls to the centre of the disc?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"150\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"200\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"250\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"300\\; \\textup{J}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
  },
